From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 21:58:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02440/11362] [outer-loop] measure the LIVE loop honestly:
 frame-only agent reaches 8/32 oracle levels (gap 24)

Operator directive ("measure the live loop honestly"): the offline GameAdapter/
OfflineSolver oracle and the LIVE frame-only path were disconnected, and the
32-levels/16-games scorecard measures the OFFLINE oracle, not live capability.

Extended scripts/arc_leaderboard_eval.py (NOT a new edifice) with --games oracle
(target the 16 oracle-reproduced games, read from ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml,
report gap = oracle_levels - live_levels) and --policy explorer|e3 (tier-1
graph_explore floor vs the full E3 world-model-induction cascade). The agent runs
with NO banked plan, NO GameAdapter, NO env._game reads -- the genuine unseen-game
simulation.

RESULT (policy=explorer, the frame-only tier-1 floor): the live path reaches
8 / 32 oracle levels -- GAP 24.
  CLOSED frame-only (6): cd82, ls20, m0r0, r11l, sp80, su15 (all L1).
  OPEN gaps (10): tn36 7, tr87 6, lp85 3, tu93 2, ar25/cn04/ka59/sc25/sk48/wa30 1 each.

Honest implications:
- The tr87 6/6 offline solve contributes ZERO live levels (frame-only reaches tr87
  L0, gap 6). The whole tr87 arc grew the OFFLINE scorecard; the live agent can do
  none of it. Concrete proof the per-game GameAdapter path is a parallel edifice.
- tn36 (7) + tr87 (6) = 13 of 24 gap-levels are deep config/rewrite games that need
  the E3 world-model-induction tier, not the explorer.
- 6 games (ar25/cn04/ka59/sc25/sk48/wa30) are gap-1 L1-FLOOR failures: the frame-only
  explorer can't even reach L1. These are the cheapest wins to target.
- This 8/32 (not 32/16) is the new north-star metric. Next: run --policy e3 to see
  whether the world-model-induction cascade closes any of the gap (the real research
  question), and target the gap-1 floor failures first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
